---
import Calls from "./Calls.astro";
import { calls, inputTokens, k } from "../samples/context.ts";

const stats = [
  { num: "26.0k", unit: "", label: "tokens, median, in context before the first reply" },
  { num: "70", unit: "%", label: "of all tokens processed went to that starting load" },
  { num: "9", unit: "/12", label: "skills listed in every session and never once used" },
];
---

<section class="problem" id="problem">
  <p class="eyebrow">Fig. 2 — The problem</p>
  <h2>The layers ride along on <em>every call.</em></h2>
  <p class="section-lede">
    Each layer is added by a different tool, plugin or file, and they pile up without anyone
    noticing. The model is stateless, so the harness resends all of it on every call, and none of it
    shows up anywhere you can see. A bloated context is one reason agents go off the rails: when one
    drifts, you can't tell whether it was missing something or buried under it.
  </p>
  <figure class="calls-figure">
    <div class="calls-scroll">
      <Calls />
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      One prompt, {calls} model calls, {calls} full windows. Each one carries the same starting
      layers; the run processed {k(inputTokens)} input tokens in all.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="stats">
    {
      stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">
            {s.num}
            <small>{s.unit}</small>
          </span>
          <span class="label">{s.label}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="footnote">Figures from the demo history behind every sample on this page.</p>
</section>
